within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.J_AntiinfectivesForSystemicUse.J01A_Tetracyclines.J01AA13_Eravacycline;
model Eravacycline_Singh2026_PD_mab_burden_8
  "sigmoid_emax exposure-response sweep — Singh_2026 :: MAB burden (MAB burden)"
  extends Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep(
    E0 = 8.204,      // [log10 CFU/mL]
    Emax = -6.576,  // [log10 CFU/mL]
    EC50 = 0.8497,  // [kg/m3; mg/L × 0.001]
    gamma = 0.5769,
    exposure_per_s = 0.001);   // 1 mg/L per second
  // imax_as_negative_emax: Imax (Q323) enters SigmoidEmaxSweep as −Emax
  annotation(experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 8500, Interval = 17),
    Documentation(info = "<html><body><h4>Eravacycline_Singh2026_PD_mab_burden_8</h4><p>The steady-state exposure-response curve of Singh S et al., <i>Microbiology spectrum 14(1):e0343225</i> 2026 (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1128/spectrum.03432-25\">doi:10.1128/spectrum.03432-25</a>) — MAB burden [log10 CFU/mL] against eravacycline mg/L — obtained by sweeping the driver instead of simulating a dose. Model family: sigmoid_emax.</p><h4>The parameters, in the paper's terms</h4><pre>  E0    =      8.204 log10 CFU/mL drug-free response (baseline) (Econ, Q324)
  Emax  =      6.576 log10 CFU/mL maximal effect term (Emax, Q323)
  EC50  =      849.7 mg/L     exposure at half of the maximal effect term (EC50, Q321)
  gamma =     0.5769          Hill coefficient (H, Q325)</pre><p>The algebra is <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep\">SigmoidEmaxSweep</a>; this model only supplies the numbers. The x axis is one mg/L of eravacycline per second of simulated time (exposure is in kg/m3): there is no state, no dose and no kinetics — plot <code>response</code> against <code>exposure</code> (or <code>time</code>).</p><h4>What it reproduces</h4><pre>  exposure = 0         response 8.204   (drug-free)
  exposure = EC50 (849.7 mg/L)  response 4.916
  exposure -> infinity  response 1.628</pre></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Singh_2026: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: curated candidate</li></ul></body></html>"));
end Eravacycline_Singh2026_PD_mab_burden_8;
